# =============================================================================
# FILE: .env.example
# PURPOSE: Documents the environment variables the AI assistant needs.
#          Copy the values into the Cloudflare Pages dashboard, NOT into a
#          committed file.
#
#          Cloudflare dashboard → Workers & Pages → 1n599-inc → Settings →
#          Variables and secrets. Set them separately for Production and
#          Preview — a variable scoped to one environment does NOT exist in the
#          other.
#
# LOCAL DEV: `wrangler pages dev` reads local values from `.dev.vars` (which is
#          gitignored). Create it by copying this file:
#              cp .env.example .dev.vars
#          then paste your real key into .dev.vars only.
# =============================================================================

# Anthropic (Claude) API key. Type: SECRET (encrypted) in the Cloudflare dashboard.
# Read ONLY by functions/api/assistant.ts, server-side. Never expose this to the
# browser and never prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-your_key_here

# Model ID. Type: plaintext variable. OPTIONAL — leave unset to use the built-in
# model chain in functions/api/assistant.ts, which is the recommended setup.
#
# Only set this to pin a specific model. It must be a current model from
# https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/models/overview. A value
# naming a known-retired model is ignored, so a stale pin cannot take the
# assistant down.
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact form. No secrets required.
#
# Mail is sent by the private Worker in workers/email (Cloudflare Email Service,
# `send_email` binding) which the Pages project reaches over the EMAIL_SERVICE
# service binding. Pages Functions cannot hold a `send_email` binding directly,
# which is the only reason that Worker exists.
#
# Deploy it with:  npm run deploy:email
# Where mail lands: CONTACT_TO in workers/email/src/index.ts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional product analytics (PostHog). Public, inlined at `next build`.
#
# This site is a static export: Cloudflare dashboard variables are NOT applied
# to JS that was already built. Set these on the machine that runs
# `npm run deploy` if you want analytics in that build.
#
# Use the 1N599 Inc PostHog project — not TheReelty's keys (phc_sSDL…).
# If unset, PostHog never loads and the consent banner still records a choice.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_your_1n599_inc_project_key
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com
